WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.010
- So how do you prepare yourself mentally

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.180
to be an entrepreneur?

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.890
So what I will say is,
maybe borrowing a little bit

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.668
from Buddhism or philosophical Hinduism,

00:00:11.668 --> 00:00:14.270
but it's really this notion

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:18.250
to try to not get attached to the outcome.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.100
Obviously you're going
into entrepreneurship

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.330
because you're imagining

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.020
that one, you could be your own boss,

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.200
you'll be able to apply
your creative ideas,

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.580
you'll be able to do a
service for the world.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.970
But it's good to go into it
with a bit of a Zen philosophy

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.440
where you're gonna do what's right,

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.101
you're gonna do what's in
service of the customer

00:00:36.101 --> 00:00:40.380
or the user or whomever you are serving.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.990
But you're not going to define yourself

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.560
based on how successful
you are or you're not.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.610
Because what typically
happens in entrepreneurship

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.580
is that you start with this optimism

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:53.860
and that's where I started too,

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.000
and it's almost delusional
or it sometimes can be,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.946
and you might quit your
job and then you go into it

00:00:59.946 --> 00:01:01.414
and you quickly realize

00:01:01.414 --> 00:01:04.620
that the world doesn't immediately

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.823
come to recognize the brilliance

00:01:06.823 --> 00:01:10.730
of what you might be working on.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.500
And so there will likely be a period

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.241
where you'll really question yourself,

00:01:14.241 --> 00:01:16.490
you'll be looking at your finances,

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.480
you'll be depleting your finances,

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:19.930
and it's all that much worse

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:23.160
if your ego is heavily
invested in that as well.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.727
And if you say, "What
will people think of me?

00:01:24.727 --> 00:01:26.667
"What is going to happen to my career?

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:27.917
"I'm not going to be able to afford

00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:30.181
"the lifestyle that I'm used to."

00:01:30.181 --> 00:01:33.620
But if you suppress your ego a little bit

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.780
and say, "I'm doing this
for the good of the world,"

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.597
whether it's for-profit,
nonprofit, whatever it is,

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:40.997
"I'm doing it in service to others,

00:01:40.997 --> 00:01:42.960
"and I'm doing what's right,"

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.570
and hopefully you will have a good outcome

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.270
but you're not super attached to it,

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:49.350
then it's going to
lower the anxiety level.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.807
I heard a quote recently that,

00:01:50.807 --> 00:01:53.326
"Anxiety is misplaced imagination."

00:01:53.326 --> 00:01:57.900
And I think most entrepreneurs,
or aspiring entrepreneurs,

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.330
the one thing they have a
surplus of is imagination

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.940
and that's a great thing,

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:04.280
but sometimes your imagination
can get into cycles

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.760
of all of the bad things that'll happen

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.360
or how people will think of
you et cetera, et cetera.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.290
So I would try not to go there.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.240
And if you do that I think
you'll just be more resilient

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.185
because a lot of entrepreneurial ideas

00:02:17.185 --> 00:02:20.710
it's not a matter of whether
it's a good idea or not,

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:22.939
it's not a matter of even

00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:25.090
whether you're executing well or not,

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.710
you do need to execute well,

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.520
but sometimes it's a matter of timing,

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.187
and the more resilient
you can make yourself,

00:02:31.187 --> 00:02:34.650
also the more resilient
you can make your business.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.310
So making yourself resilient

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.580
and we're talking about mental resilience,

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.403
you can make yourself
financially resilient,

00:02:39.403 --> 00:02:42.541
by living below your means,
having a lot of savings,

00:02:42.541 --> 00:02:46.600
and you can make your
business financially resilient

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.790
so that it can hit the
timing at the right time

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.285
or have more time to be able to,

00:02:51.285 --> 00:02:54.240
for the market to recognize its value,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.500
if you do it in a very lean way

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.350
and if you're always
taking new data points

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:00.380
and processing it.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.240
And that's another place

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.490
where it's good to suppress your ego

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.630
'cause sometimes early on you
get so enamored with an idea,

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:08.600
that even if some data
points, even if some research,

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.320
even if some customers are telling you

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.590
that aah, it's not exactly what they want,

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:14.257
you're confirmation bias is almost like,

00:03:14.257 --> 00:03:15.377
"Well I'm talking to the wrong people,

00:03:15.377 --> 00:03:16.780
"or that data might not be right,"

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:17.963
and maybe that's the case,

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:20.430
but I think the less
that you have your ego

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.490
super invested in your idea,

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:23.930
that it's your idea,

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.420
the more that you'll be willing to pivot,

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.470
and the more that you're
willing to change.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.290
Famously in the early days of Khan Academy

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.600
when I was working on all of the software

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.470
I showed it to a friend

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.280
and he suggested that I make videos

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.430
to supplement the software

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.580
and I immediately thought
it was a horrible idea,

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.520
but it took a little bit
of my ego suppression

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.050
to realize that just
because I didn't think of it

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.320
doesn't mean it's a bad idea,

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.750
and just because other people had done it

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.640
doesn't mean it was a bad idea,

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.010
so I said, "Let me try it out,"

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.910
and there was a unique
take on how I was doing it

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:51.150
to complement the software

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:54.130
that that very nascent
Khan Academy was doing

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:58.441
that really helped us get off the ground.

00:03:58.441 --> 00:04:01.280
So what I would say is become resilient,

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.020
a look that is being aware of your ego,

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.780
you don't have to destroy your ego,

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.280
but know it's there,

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.250
and you have to put it in
it's place every now and then.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.720
Always be open to new data,

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.470
make yourself financially
and mentally resilient

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:15.900
and do the same for your organization

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.323
or your nascent organization
that you're starting.

